{#
settings/templates/_tree.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The template tree: top-level templates, then one folder per mail account, then
the folders the user made beside them.

The account folders are always drawn, empty ones included. That is the feature
— the tree mirrors the accounts — and an account that only appeared once it
held something would give a new user a tree with nothing in it and no hint of
where a template for one address is meant to go.

Every row that opens something is a link into the `template-editor` frame, so
the tree works with JavaScript off and needs no controller of its own.

Variables:
  tree  App\Domain\DTO\Template\TemplateTree
#}
{% set action = "inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-2.5 h-8 rounded-lg text-xs font-medium transition-colors cursor-pointer" %}

<div class="flex items-center justify-end gap-2 px-3 py-3 border-b border-line bg-sunken">
    <a href="{{ path('app_settings_templates_folder_new') }}"
       data-turbo-frame="template-editor"
       class="{{ action }} bg-field border border-field text-ink-soft hover:bg-hover">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-folder-plus text-[10px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        {{ 'settings.templates.add_folder'|trans }}
    </a>
    <a href="{{ path('app_settings_templates_new') }}"
       data-turbo-frame="template-editor"
       class="{{ action }} bg-accent hover:bg-accent-strong text-accent-ink">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-plus text-[10px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        {{ 'settings.templates.add'|trans }}
    </a>
</div>

<nav aria-label="{{ 'settings.templates.heading'|trans }}" class="p-2">
    {% if tree.empty %}
        <p class="px-2 pt-2 pb-3 text-xs text-ink-faint">{{ 'settings.templates.empty'|trans }}</p>
    {% endif %}

    {% if tree.templates|length %}
        <ul class="pb-1.5 mb-1.5 border-b border-line">
            {% for template in tree.templates %}
                {% include 'settings/templates/_tree_template.html.twig' with { template: template } only %}
            {% endfor %}
        </ul>
    {% endif %}

    <ul>
        {% for node in tree.accounts %}
            {% include 'settings/templates/_tree_node.html.twig' with { node: node } only %}
        {% endfor %}
        {% for node in tree.folders %}
            {% include 'settings/templates/_tree_node.html.twig' with { node: node } only %}
        {% endfor %}
    </ul>
</nav>
